<%# decor/app/views/storage_locations/_form.html.erb - version 1.0 %>
<%# Session B (Storage Locations feature). %>
<%#
Single-field form: name (VARCHAR(50), unique per owner — see
storage_location.rb v1.0's uniqueness: { scope: :owner_id } validation). No
collection_select / Tom Select needed — just one text field.

Submit label is explicit (not the f.submit model-class-name default) per
DECOR_PROJECT.md Design Patterns ("Primary: descriptive — 'Update Computer',
'Save Component'") and RAILS_SPECIFICS.md's "UI Renames" caution about
f.submit's auto-generated label — "Create Storage location" / "Update
Storage location" (note the lowercase "location") is what Rails would
generate from the class name; using an explicit string avoids that entirely
rather than relying on a coincidence of capitalization.

"Done" always returns to the index — there is no show page (routes.rb v3.8
excludes :show), so persisted? doesn't change the Done target the way it
does in software_items/_form.html.erb.
%>

<%= form_with model: storage_location, class: "space-y-4" do |f| %>
  <%= render "common/record_errors", record: storage_location %>

  <div>
    <%= f.label :name, "Name", class: "block text-sm font-medium text-stone-700" %>
    <%= f.text_field :name, maxlength: 50, placeholder: "e.g. Attic Shelf 3", class: field_classes %>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-stone-500">Maximum 50 characters. Must be unique among your own storage locations.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex gap-3">
    <%= f.submit(storage_location.persisted? ? "Update Storage Location" : "Add Storage Location",
          class: button_classes(style: :primary)) %>
    <%# "Done" — never "Cancel" (project convention: DECOR_PROJECT.md Design Patterns). %>
    <%= link_to "Done", storage_locations_path, class: button_classes(style: :secondary) %>
  </div>
<% end %>
